ce would greatly improve the odds  for the kingdom and that is without  taking into account that he's also able  to activate shika towers and other  important technology which  also made a huge difference on the  outcome and may or may not have been  planned by the queen as well  which brings us to tarico as a character  it's clear that despite his programming  the guardian has a distinct personality  of his own  he's very playful bold and interruptive  especially towards impa  and even a bit passive aggressive on  some occasions like when he gets angry  at link for ruining his opportunity to  save zelda himself he even seems a bit  jealous of link and zelda's relationship  at times  though for reasons i will mention later  i don't think this has any romantic  motivations on the side of the guardian  but it's clear that tereko also  performed certain actions without being  conscious about it which makes sense  since if it's something pre-programmed  into him by zelda's mother  he himself wouldn't know why he's doing  it he's simply  executing a protocol i think this is  most evident from the scene we talked  about earlier  after getting hit by zelda's tear and  doing his little time shenanigans we can  clearly see that he is just as confused  as everyone else about what just  happened  almost as if shrugging his shoulders and  being like hey guys  i don't know either when he's just  hanging around the group he is acting  upon his  own personality however when he executes  one of these protocols  that is in a sense zelda's mother  forcing him to do whatever is needed  that includes opening the portal and  jumping back in time at the very  beginning of the game  so to paint a broader picture tarako  sits dormant on a shelf for 11 years  detects the presence of the divine power  and activates itself  as mentioned before zelda's mother knew  that zelda would eventually awaken her  power but wasn't sure if this was going  to be in time to save the kingdom  this means that tereco was programmed to  deal with two different scenarios in  breath of the wild's timeline  had zelda awakened her power in time the  war against ganon could have been won  she would have sealed ganon successfully  as was the original plan  or she would have been too late and the  kingdom would already be destroyed along  with everyone in it  tereko would have awakened either way  since in both scenarios the divine power  is  activated at some point the guardian  would then assess the situation  if hyrul has been saved he basically  doesn't have to do anything  however as we all know this is not how  things panned out  instead he wakes up sees the kingdom in  ruin and executes the time travel  protocol  jumps into the portal and the events of  age of calamity pick up  but we're not done yet there's one final  thing we need to address before rounding  up this theory  since if we're talking about terrico we  of course also have to mention his  doppelganger  harbinger ganon  despite this brilliant plan set up by  zelda's mother ganon had a plan of his  own and took swift countermeasures  since terrico jumped into the past this  of course means that in this new reality  there are now two terracotes one from  the present and the age of calamity  timeline  and one from the future aka breath of  the wild's timeline  the moment tariko jumps into the time  portal the demon king catapults slivers  of his malice into the portal right on  the heels  of the guardian turns out that this  malice ultimately landed on the terraco  from the present  this version of the tiny guardian is  literally possessed by ganon from breath  of the wild's timeline and because that  cannon is from the future  it in turn knows the future and is given  the name  harbinger gannon harbinger then  approaches astor to act as his mediator  and his puppet to impose his will and  strategies  this is why ganon is even more powerful  in age of calamity than he was in breath  of the wild  the knowledge of the future through  terraco didn't just benefit the heroes  of the story but also  their adversary it wasn't enough for  ganon to succeed in one timeline  and wanted to assure that hyrule met its  downfall in every branch of reality  if you finish the game which let's be  honest you probably have if you're  watching this video you already know how  the story concludes so i'm not going to  explain it in any finer detail  but what i will touch upon is that even  though this is by no means the most  original premise i do find it very  poetic how the duality between these two  guardians  is the very backbone of the story  because when you really think about it  if terico was indeed programmed by  zelda's mother  a being who possessed the power of the  goddess hylia and harbinger gannon is  well ganon that means that in a sense  this is a battle between the demon king  and goddess hylia  represented by the queen of hyrule not  in the literal sense of course  since it is still just a machine but a  machine that was quite literally  designed to do  what zelda's mother couldn't do in her  absence you could even draw a parallel  between this game  and terminator 2. if you've ever seen  that movie the premise of age of  calamity  may feel very familiar to you in this  story the world has been destroyed in a  cataclysmic event by skynet  a computer program which achieved  consciousness and deemed all humans to  be a threat to the planet  and its own existence only a small  sliver of humans still remains  which under the leadership of john  connor manages to persevere into  fighting back against the machines  as a way to deal with this last  resistance skynet sends a terminator  a machine designed to look human back in  time in an attempt to kill conor when  he's still a young boy  as a counter-measure the resistance  leader sends his own terminator which he  reprogrammed to protect his younger self  at all costs  so we have two machines from the future  one set to destroy and the other  to protect of course in age of  calamity's case it's zelda's mother who  programmed it and not  zelda herself but you gotta admit that  there are some very strong similarities  here  during the climax of age of calamity our  heroes are  somehow unable to hurt ganon despite the  master sword and even the sacred power  it's still not enough to win the fight  but we again  see terraco reawaken and reacting to the  divine power  and again it does what it was programmed  to do protects zelda and her kingdom at  all cost  heavily damaged and with all other  options exhausted  it makes a final sacrifice to help  destroy the evil that has plagued hyrule  for millennia  with this sacrifice ganon is now  rendered  vulnerable another testament that this  really was the queen of hyrule's doing  since  who else than zelda's mother could  actually hurt ganon  even after the master sword failed if  there wasn't some essence of her power  left in this little machine  in the final memory of zelda we see that  on the night of the queen's death  she gazes at a shooting star up in the  sky  she then calls out to her mother and  almost immediately  tarako starts playing zelda's lullaby  though she has passed  zelda's mother was never truly gone an  essence of her  lived on within zelda's companion all  throughout the story events of age of  calamity we see this reflected back on  tarako's behavior  being suspective of link when it  observes the chemistry between him and  zelda  as any mother would in a situation like  that this isn't jealousy  it's trying to protect her from possible  heartbreak but as link proves his  worthiness and his devotion  the guardian slowly accepts him  basically deeming him worthy of her  affection  we can even see it boldly trying to talk  sense into zelda's father  almost as if the queen herself is  indirectly trying to tell her husband to  go easy on their daughter  and be less strict with her of course  the king unable to understand what it  says  simply stares back at it in confusion  though we didn't get to see much of  zelda's mother in the flesh  there's a case to be made that in a  sense she was actually one of  if not the most important character in  the story  of age of calamity  if you want to see more about the queen  of hyrule and her history  please be sure to check out the video  made by commonwealth realm which is  basically a sister video to this one  the link will be in the description and  in the end card so  go check it out it's good thank you all  for watching and  have a great day  you
 

